{% schema %}
  {
    
    "name": "Section 3",
    "tag": "section",
    "class": "gps-635745675807621798 gps gpsil",
    "settings": [{"type":"paragraph","content":"Section design by GemPages. [Click here to start design](https://admin.shopify.com/store/photobrickusa/apps/gempages-cro/app/shopify/edit?pageType=GP_ARTICLE&editorId=635745675656561318&sectionId=635745675807621798)"},{"type":"select","label":"Section Preload","id":"section_preload","options":[{"label":"On","value":"true"},{"label":"Off","value":"false"},{"label":"Off Lazy Script","value":"off_lazy_script"}],"default":"false"},{"type":"text","label":"Checksum","id":"checksum"},{"type":"html","id":"ggWi0E6lAfS_text","label":"ggWi0E6lAfS_text","default":"<p>A finished piece of artwork can be impressive, but there is something special about knowing you watched it come together from the very beginning.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>A table covered with tiny bricks may not look like much at first. There is no recognizable picture yet, no finished composition, and no obvious centerpiece for the wall. Just pieces, colors, and the beginning of a project.</p><p>Then you place one piece.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Then another.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>A small section begins to form. Shapes start appearing. Colors connect. Eventually, what looked like a collection of tiny bricks starts becoming something you recognize.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>That is the experience behind brick mosaic art. It is not just about what you see when the project is finished. It is about watching something come to life one piece at a time.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggYfPM1SNQS_text","label":"ggYfPM1SNQS_text","default":"<p>Every Piece Has a Place</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggrfu9Sl95Q_text","label":"ggrfu9Sl95Q_text","default":"<p>One of the interesting things about building a mosaic is how important every small piece becomes.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>A single brick might not seem significant on its own. But placed next to hundreds of others, it becomes part of a larger picture.</p><p>This is what makes the building process so engaging. You are constantly looking at small details while knowing that those details are contributing to something much bigger.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>A section might contain only a few colors at first. As more pieces are added, the shapes begin to make sense. What seemed random starts becoming intentional.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>By the time the mosaic is complete, those individual pieces have worked together to create one unified image.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggIyFqM9oJN_text","label":"ggIyFqM9oJN_text","default":"<p>The Fun Is in Watching It Change</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggrNCTIcwED_srcSet_desktop_src","label":"ggrNCTIcwED_srcSet_desktop_src","default":"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0375/0107/5595/files/94de4746-a3a9-4e7d-accd-882977eab301.png"},{"type":"html","id":"ggrNCTIcwED_alt","label":"ggrNCTIcwED_alt","default":"Memobrick Photo  Mosaic Gift Idea"},{"type":"html","id":"ggrNCTIcwED_title","label":"ggrNCTIcwED_title","default":"Memobrick Photo  Mosaic Gift Idea"},{"type":"html","id":"gg8DZ8toEDb_text","label":"gg8DZ8toEDb_text","default":"<p>A brick mosaic does not reveal everything immediately.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>That is part of what makes it fun.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>You begin with a project that requires you to focus on individual sections. As you continue building, recognizable features slowly appear. You might suddenly notice an outline, a color pattern, or a familiar detail that was not obvious before.</p><p>Every completed section gives you another glimpse of the final result.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>It creates a natural feeling of progress. You can look at what you have already built and see that the image is getting closer with every step.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Instead of waiting until the end to appreciate the artwork, you get to enjoy small moments of discovery throughout the entire process.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggjBxHO5SWu_text","label":"ggjBxHO5SWu_text","default":"<p>A Project You Can Take at Your Own Pace</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggAGDP2-GP1_text","label":"ggAGDP2-GP1_text","default":"<p>Not every creative project needs to be completed in one sitting.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Sometimes the best part is having something you can return to.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>You can build for an hour, step away, and come back later. You can complete one section before dinner and continue another day. You can work slowly and carefully or challenge yourself to see how much you can finish in one session.</p><p>There is no need to rush the process.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>A brick mosaic can become a relaxing weekend project, an evening activity, or something you work on whenever you have time. The flexibility makes it easy to fit into different routines.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>And when you eventually finish, you can look back at the progress and see just how far you came.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggDyQBfs6E7_text","label":"ggDyQBfs6E7_text","default":"<p>From Simple Pieces to a Bigger Picture</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggnABjU9y2r_text","label":"ggnABjU9y2r_text","default":"<p>The magic of mosaic art comes from perspective.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Up close, you see the individual bricks. You notice their shape, color, placement, and texture.</p><p>Move farther away, and those small details begin working together.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The image becomes easier to recognize.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>That change in perspective is one of the most interesting characteristics of brick mosaic art. It gives the finished piece two different visual experiences. You can appreciate the overall image from across the room while still discovering the construction details when you move closer.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The result is artwork that rewards curiosity.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggCD-7SHqUV_text","label":"ggCD-7SHqUV_text","default":"<p>Building Can Be Better Than Simply Buying</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg_MYVq_hsX_text","label":"gg_MYVq_hsX_text","default":"<p>There is a difference between receiving something finished and creating something yourself.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>When a piece arrives already completed, you can immediately enjoy the result. But when you build it yourself, the finished artwork also represents the time you invested in creating it.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>You remember the beginning.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>You remember the sections that gradually came together.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>You remember the moment when the image finally became recognizable.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>And you remember placing the last piece.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>That process gives the finished artwork another layer of value. It is not only something you can look at. It is something you experienced.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggo-bqvBRUy_text","label":"ggo-bqvBRUy_text","default":"<p>Brick Art Is Creative Without Being Complicated</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggMEhcb4Tz3_text","label":"ggMEhcb4Tz3_text","default":"<p>You do not need to be an experienced artist to enjoy creating a brick mosaic.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>You do not need a paintbrush, drawing tablet, or years of artistic training.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The beauty of the process is that the design gives you a path to follow. Your job is to organize the pieces, follow the pattern, and build the artwork gradually.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>That makes brick art approachable for people who enjoy creative activities but may not consider themselves artists.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>There is still plenty of room for patience, organization, concentration, and creativity. You simply experience those things through building rather than drawing or painting.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggOdwHyQeJX_text","label":"ggOdwHyQeJX_text","default":"<p>Something Everyone Can Contribute To</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggIbs2XB63J_text","label":"ggIbs2XB63J_text","default":"<p>One of the best things about building with small pieces is that it can become a shared activity.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Instead of everyone sitting separately with their own screens, a brick mosaic can give people something to work on together.</p><p>One person can sort colors. Someone else can assemble a section. Another person can check the pattern and help find the next pieces.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>For families, couples, or friends, the project can become an easy way to spend time together while working toward the same finished result.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>And when the artwork is complete, everyone involved can look at it and say, \"We built that.\"</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggG5mbQXtNr_text","label":"ggG5mbQXtNr_text","default":"<p>Choosing the Right Scale for Your Artwork</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggXzyTizxPl_text","label":"ggXzyTizxPl_text","default":"<p>The size of a mosaic can make a noticeable difference in how much detail can be represented.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Smaller sizes are great when the design is simple and the subject does not require a lot of visual information. Larger sizes provide more space for additional details and can make complex subjects easier to recognize.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>For example, a close up portrait can work well in a smaller format, while subjects such as cars, motorcycles, pets, or larger scenes may benefit from additional space.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>For vehicles in particular, sizes such as 30x20 or 40x30 can give the design more room to show important details and the overall shape of the subject.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The goal is to choose a size that gives your artwork enough room to become the image you want it to be.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggPe-1y1mF8_text","label":"ggPe-1y1mF8_text","default":"<p>There Is Something Satisfying About Finishing</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg7L0VZT7aW_text","label":"gg7L0VZT7aW_text","default":"<p>Eventually, there is only one piece left.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>You place it into position.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>You look over the entire mosaic.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>And suddenly, the project is complete.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>That final moment can be surprisingly satisfying because you have watched the artwork develop from an empty workspace into something recognizable and finished.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>You can see every section you worked through and every small piece that contributed to the final image.</p><p>The satisfaction does not come only from having a finished piece of art.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>It comes from knowing that you built it.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggUcxttLlSn_text","label":"ggUcxttLlSn_text","default":"<p>Memobrick starts with an image, but the finished result is something completely different.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Instead of leaving the image on a phone or computer screen, it becomes a physical mosaic made from individual bricks.</p><p>Technology helps us create the design, while people carefully review the result to make sure the final artwork works well as a brick mosaic.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Technology helps us create it. People make sure we get it right.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>That combination turns a digital image into something you can physically interact with, build, and eventually display.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggofiL611Vj_text","label":"ggofiL611Vj_text","default":"CUSTOMER'S REVIEW"},{"type":"html","id":"ggEoX4GWeEB_srcSet_desktop_src","label":"ggEoX4GWeEB_srcSet_desktop_src","default":"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0375/0107/5595/files/John_R._It_was_a_fun_relaxing_task._My_wife_and_I_are_thrilled_to_have_our_wedding_photo_in_such_an_interesting_style.jpg"},{"type":"html","id":"ggEoX4GWeEB_alt","label":"ggEoX4GWeEB_alt","default":"Customize Memobrick Gift Idea"},{"type":"html","id":"ggEoX4GWeEB_title","label":"ggEoX4GWeEB_title","default":"Customize Memobrick Gift Idea"},{"type":"html","id":"ggii5080P9G_text","label":"ggii5080P9G_text","default":"<p><strong>John R.</strong></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gglcGgYBoAb_text","label":"gglcGgYBoAb_text","default":"<p>&nbsp;It was a fun relaxing task. My wife and I are thrilled to have our wedding photo in such an interesting style</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggr3vAGbYwy_srcSet_desktop_src","label":"ggr3vAGbYwy_srcSet_desktop_src","default":"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0375/0107/5595/files/Aaryn_C._So_easy_to_understand_and_a_nice_relaxing_project_for_my_free_time._Can_t_wait_to_do_another_one.jpg"},{"type":"html","id":"ggr3vAGbYwy_alt","label":"ggr3vAGbYwy_alt","default":"Customize Memobrick Gift Idea"},{"type":"html","id":"ggr3vAGbYwy_title","label":"ggr3vAGbYwy_title","default":"Customize Memobrick Gift Idea"},{"type":"html","id":"ggjBA9EPd6S_text","label":"ggjBA9EPd6S_text","default":"<p><strong>Aaryn C.</strong></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggpWaWSEt8h_text","label":"ggpWaWSEt8h_text","default":"<p>So easy to understand and a nice relaxing project for my free time. Can't wait to do another one!</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggL5y_Oy0ur_srcSet_desktop_src","label":"ggL5y_Oy0ur_srcSet_desktop_src","default":"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0375/0107/5595/files/Candice_L._I_split_the_photo_in_half_so_I_could_get_2_of_the_60x20_so_I_could_fill_my_wall_more_and_its_turned_out_AMAZING.jpg"},{"type":"html","id":"ggL5y_Oy0ur_alt","label":"ggL5y_Oy0ur_alt","default":"Customize Memobrick Gift Idea"},{"type":"html","id":"ggL5y_Oy0ur_title","label":"ggL5y_Oy0ur_title","default":"Customize Memobrick Gift Idea"},{"type":"html","id":"ggUZSTpM54b_text","label":"ggUZSTpM54b_text","default":"<p><strong>Candice L.</strong></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggl5uJy7tO1_text","label":"ggl5uJy7tO1_text","default":"<p>I split the photo in half so I could get 2 of the 60x20 so I could fill my wall more and its turned out AMAZING!</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg2qLRyhJkY_srcSet_desktop_src","label":"gg2qLRyhJkY_srcSet_desktop_src","default":"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0375/0107/5595/files/Jennifer_H._Was_a_fun_and_a_little_bit_challenging_project_to_do._Can_t_wait_to_do_another_one.jpg"},{"type":"html","id":"gg2qLRyhJkY_alt","label":"gg2qLRyhJkY_alt","default":"Customize Memobrick Gift Idea"},{"type":"html","id":"gg2qLRyhJkY_title","label":"gg2qLRyhJkY_title","default":"Customize Memobrick Gift Idea"},{"type":"html","id":"ggYWvnOapW__text","label":"ggYWvnOapW__text","default":"<p><strong>Jennifer H.</stro